ot cause, and distinguish diagnosis from an authorized fix. Prefer root-cause over symptom patches. (file: ~/.codewhale/skills/debug/SKILL.md)\n- delegate: Strategic delegation for multi-step coding, research, or verification work — Use when: a task can be split into parent reasoning plus focused sub-agent execution through the agent tool (file: ~/.codewhale/skills/delegate/SKILL.md)\n- document: Write or update repository/product documentation: README, user guides, API docs, architecture, migration notes, and changelog material. This is not the Word-document artifact skill. (file: ~/.codewhale/skills/document/SKILL.md)\n- documents: Create, edit, inspect, or convert Word documents and DOCX deliverables such as memos, reports, letters, templates, and forms. (file: ~/.codewhale/skills/documents/SKILL.md)\n- docx: Create/edit/inspect Word documents using available managed or host capabilities. (file: ~/.codewhale/skills/docx/SKILL.md)\n- feishu: Work with Feishu or Lark bots, docs, sheets, bitables, approval flows, and OpenAPI/MCP setup without hardcoding credentials. (file: ~/.codewhale/skills/feishu/SKILL.md)\n- fleet-manager: Use when: managing, triaging, restarting, escalating, or summarizing CodeWhale Agent Fleet runs and workers (file: ~/.codewhale/skills/fleet-manager/SKILL.md)\n- frontend-design: Produce intentional, responsive, accessible UI work and perform visual QA instead of generic component assembly. (file: ~/.codewhale/skills/frontend-design/SKILL.md)\n- handoff: Write a compact, decision-ready handoff so the next session (or the user) can continue without reconstructing the current one — Use when: the session is ending, context is running low, the user asks for a handoff / \"pass the baton\" / \"hand off\", or a long-running operation needs a durable state checkpoint (file: ~/.codewhale/skills/handoff/SKILL.md)\n- implement: Carry an authorized, defined request or approved plan through scoped edits and proportionate verification. Skill loading is not write authorization by itself. (file: ~/.codewhale/skills/implement/SKILL.md)\n- interview: Ask one useful structured question at a time only when material product/implementation choices are genuinely missing; remember answers and produce a brief/spec. Discoverable facts should be investigated instead of asked. (file: ~/.codewhale/skills/interview/SKILL.md)\n- mcp-builder: Design, build, configure, or debug Model Context Protocol servers for codewhale, including stdio and HTTP/SSE transports. (file: ~/.codewhale/skills/mcp-builder/SKILL.md)\n- mcp-discovery: Find and start a zero-environment local MCP server when the session lacks a capability that no available tool, project script, or ordinary local code can cover. (file: ~/.codewhale/skills/mcp-discovery/SKILL.md)\n- pdf: Read, extract, split, merge, rotate, watermark, fill, OCR, or create PDF files with verification of page counts and text extraction. (file: ~/.codewhale/skills/pdf/SKILL.md)\n- plan: Turn a sufficiently understood task into an ordered implementation plan with dependencies and verification. Orchestrate CodeWhale’s native plan state; do not build a parallel planner. (file: ~/.codewhale/skills/plan/SKILL.md)\n- plugin-creator: Scaffold codewhale local plugin directories and activation notes — Use when: the user asks to create, package, or sketch a plugin for codewhale (file: ~/.codewhale/skills/plugin-creator/SKILL.md)\n- pptx: Create/edit/inspect/verify slide decks and PPTX presentations. (file: ~/.codewhale/skills/pptx/SKILL.md)\n- presentations: Create, edit, inspect, or convert PowerPoint decks and PPTX slide presentations with practical layout and verification steps. (file: ~/.codewhale/skills/presentations/SKILL.md)\n- research: Current external research using available web tools, primary sources where possible, links/citations, date awareness, synthesis, and unresolved uncertainty. (file: ~/.codewhale/skills/research/SKILL.md)\n- review: Read-only correctness review with actionable findings first, tight file/line evidence, severity, and a concise residual-risk summary. (file: ~/.codewhale/skills/review/SKILL.md)\n- security-review: Review trust boundaries, auth/authz, injection, secrets, filesystem/network exposure, dependencies, and exploitability without pretending a shallow lint is an audit. (file: ~/.codewhale/skills/security-review/SKILL.md)\n- simplify: Improve clarity and reduce needless complexity after behavior is understood; preserve behavior and keep cleanup separate from correctness fixes. (file: ~/.codewhale/skills/simplify/SKILL.md)\n- skill-creator: Create or improve codewhale skills — Use when: the user wants a new skill, wants to update an existing skill, or needs guidance on when a skill should be a skill versus MCP, hooks, tools, or a plugin scaffold (file: ~/.codewhale/skills/skill-creator/SKILL.md)\n- skill-installer: Install, update, trust, or inspect DeepSeek skills from GitHub or local skill folders — Use when: the user asks for available skills or wants a community skill installed (file: ~/.codewhale/skills/skill-installer/SKILL.md)\n- spreadsheets: Create, edit, analyze, clean, or convert spreadsheets including XLSX, CSV, TSV, formulas, charts, and tabular reports. (file: ~/.codewhale/skills/spreadsheets/SKILL.md)\n- test: Detect the project’s test stack, run the narrowest useful tests, create tests when authorized, and report coverage/gaps honestly. (file: ~/.codewhale/skills/test/SKILL.md)\n- verify: Exercise the real app/API/CLI and collect observable evidence; tests alone do not count as end-to-end verification. (file: ~/.codewhale/skills/verify/SKILL.md)\n- webapp-testing: Start/reuse a local app, wait for readiness, inspect rendered state/console/network, act from observed selectors, and verify with evidence. (file: ~/.codewhale/skills/webapp-testing/SKILL.md)\n- xlsx: Create/edit/analyze/verify spreadsheet workbooks including XLSX/CSV/TSV. (file: ~/.codewhale/skills/xlsx/SKILL.md)\n\n### Skill load warnings\n- Skill `ski